# Hosted PostgreSQL (Neon) — the Prisma datasource provider is "postgresql".
#
# Copy the FULL string from the Neon console: project → Connect → Connection string
# (branch: your main branch, database: neondb, role: neondb_owner, pooling OFF).
# It looks like the example below — one line, no spaces, exactly one "@":
#
#   postgresql://neondb_owner:npg_AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUvWx@
#   ep-cool-name-123456.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
#
# Keep it on ONE line when you paste it into .env — the break above is only for
# readability here. Do not put "psql -h" or the word REGION in it.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://neondb_owner:npg_AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUvWx@ep-cool-name-123456.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"

# Optional: set to "1" to close self-registration (see /api/auth/register-status).
# REGISTRATION_CLOSED="1"
